      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does that mean the HAL should stop reporting this value?\n\nIf so can you add a VTS test (maybe in a separate CL) that checks that they should not be returned for health version V2 and above?\n\n--\n\nAnd same for OVERHEAT / COLD; for functions that used to return them, should they return `BatteryHealth.FAIR` instead (or maybe some other value?), and return the temperature information via BatteryChargingState? (If so / not, please document the behavior expected on the HAL.)\n\nAnd maybe in a separate CL add a VTS test that OVERHEAT / COLD should not be returned for health V2 and above.\n\n--\n\nAlso sorry I forgot to mention -- please say the version on which it is deprecated:\n\n```\n@deprecated Deprecated at version 2. Transitory condition that only affects charging.\n```",
